7. Azure Blob Storage (images)
Part 3 also covers images.

Example, organiser uploads an event banner:

MVC
 ↓
Part 2 API
 ↓
Azure Blob Storage
 ↓
Image URL
 ↓
MVC displays the image

Also, MVC should not directly connect to Azure Blob Storage. That upload handling is done by the Part 2 API.

RaceDay_Part_3_MVC_Complete_Document.docx

8. Docker
Part 3 also has to run in a Docker container.

The Dockerfile builds the MVC app, then runs the published ASP.NET app.

The document idea is like:

RaceDayMVC
     ↓
Docker
     ↓
Container
     ↓
Running web application

The container port used in the document is 8080, so keep that in mind.

