“Part 3 is the MVC web application for RaceDay. The MVC front end communicates with the Part 2 API instead of connecting directly to the database. It allows organisers and participants to use different features based on their roles. It also includes session authentication, image handling through the API and Azure Blob Storage, Docker, responsive UI design, and GitHub Actions for building and testing the application.”

And if they ask “What is the purpose of MVC?”, say:

“MVC separates the application into Models, Views and Controllers. This makes the project easier to organise and maintain. The View is what the user sees, the Controller handles requests and logic, and the Model represents the data.”

MY Part 3 checklist (one line)
MVC → API connection → Login/session → Organiser → Participant → Images/Azure → Docker → UI → GitHub Actions → README/demo.


